;; The consolidated pod context/skill loadout manifest — read by seon.config
;; via aero (`SEON_CONFIG` overrides the path; `#profile` selects a per-cluster
;; variant from `SEON_PROFILE`). ABSENT → the pod boots byte-identically to a
;; no-config world (full env-dir skill scan + default-seed-blocks). PRESENT →
;; the OPTIONAL override below. Every key fully namespaced; entries that ride
;; registered schemas (a loadout's :seon.config/blocks → :seon.agent.ctx/block)
;; are those maps verbatim. Add a new concern = add ONE key here + a resolver in
;; seon.config (the "add more things to it" contract).
{;; ── TWO SYSTEMS, DIFFERENT JOBS (owner 2026-06-28: "I want both active") ──
 ;; • The DIRECTORY is the CORPUS: the env-dir scan (`SEON_SKILLS_DIR`, default
 ;;   `seon-skills/`) loads ALL skills it finds. Dev/Claude-Code skills
 ;;   (browser-automation, clojure-testing) live PHYSICALLY separate in
 ;;   `.claude/skills/` — they are not in the agent corpus dir, so nothing here
 ;;   needs to exclude them (the directory split already does).
 ;; • This CONFIG is the OVERRIDE: ABSENT → directory loads all (byte-identical
 ;;   no-config boot). PRESENT → it curates the env-dir scan PER CLUSTER
 ;;   (`SEON_CONFIG` path, `SEON_PROFILE` #profile, `#env` interpolation). A
 ;;   `:seon.config/skills` `include`/`exclude` here is for per-cluster corpus
 ;;   curation (e.g. a test cluster trimming the corpus) — NOT for dropping dev
 ;;   skills. We ship none by default: the `seon-skills/` dir IS the agent corpus.

 ;; ── LLM PROVIDER is NOT set in this manifest ──
 ;; The agent's LLM provider/model is its OWN env→DB surface (`seon.ai`, the
 ;; `:seon.ai/config` row), deliberately separate from this loadout manifest
 ;; (see seon.config — env seeds the row once, then it is DB-owned). Select the
 ;; provider via env (e.g. in .env), not here:
 ;;   SEON_AI_PROVIDER=diffusiongemma            ; deepseek (default) | anthropic
 ;;   SEON_DG_ENDPOINT=<runpod-endpoint-id>      ;   | openai-compat | diffusiongemma
 ;;   RUNPOD_API_KEY=<key>
 ;; Full var docs: .env.example (DIFFUSIONGEMMA block). A live switch is a
 ;; transact: {:seon.ai/id "config" :seon.ai/provider :diffusiongemma}.

 ;; ── ALWAYS-ON SKILL BODIES — EXPLICIT LISTING (#42, retires the opaque
 ;; `#profile {:default … :minimal …}` skill SETS the owner rejected). The list
 ;; IS the policy — you SEE it, no profile name to decode:
 ;;   :seon.config/load :all        → every corpus skill body always-on
 ;;   :seon.config/load [:repl …]   → only these (the VISIBLE lean list)
 ;;   :seon.config/load []          → none
 ;; `:repl`'s body is always-on for EVERY agent (seeded as a :skill/repl block
 ;; at the cached-prefix priority 16). To go lean, point SEON_CONFIG at a
 ;; manifest with a shorter list (e.g. config/lean.edn) — runtime EDN, no
 ;; rebuild, just restart.
 :seon.config/skills {:seon.config/load [:repl]}

 ;; ── NAMESPACES render policy — the EXPLICIT list of WHICH nses render in the
 ;; agent prompt BODY (#42, the context lever; retires the hardcoded
 ;; full-source-whitelist / verb-signature-whitelist / my.*-always-full rules).
 ;; SIGNATURES ARE RETIRED: every rendered ns shows its REAL FULL SOURCE — the
 ;; budget is bound by CURATION (which nses), never compression (how each):
 ;;   :seon.config/always     → the always-present FULL-source nses
 ;;   :seon.config/current-ns → :full (default — the agent's own ns) | :off
 ;; The agent's current ns + the nses it :require's (with stored full source) +
 ;; third-party (acme) code render full ON TOP of this list; everything else
 ;; (framework bulk + the non-reachable my.* long tail) is DROPPED (still
 ;; indexed + grep-able). The toolkit + the core verb nses stay FULL: a
 ;; composition verb shown only as a name is undiscoverable. Trim `:always` to
 ;; a short list to go lean. (Mirrors seon.config/default-namespaces-policy.)
 :seon.config/namespaces
 {:seon.config/always     [my.kb my.data my.ui my.tile
                           seon.agent.todo seon.agent.message seon.agent.lifecycle]
  :seon.config/current-ns :full}

 ;; ── AGENT-CONTEXT (v3, config-driven-agent-init) — the two-level context
 ;; config the GENERIC loader (seon.config/resolve-agent-context) consumes. A
 ;; sparse map: every unspecified key (incl. the whole :seon.agent/ctx block
 ;; tree) is filled from its schema :default by the recursive
 ;; default-value-transformer, so `{}` reproduces the byte-parity default. Add a
 ;; key here only to DIFFER from the default (e.g. a lean block set, a per-agent
 ;; scalar). Empty = byte-identical to the no-config default tree.
 :seon.config/agent-context {}

 ;; ── ROOT-CONTEXT — a SPARSE override merged over :seon.config/agent-context
 ;; by IDENTITY (id "root"), block upsert-by-:seon.agent.ctx/name. The :live-tile
 ;; block sets root's canvas = the system/fleet dashboard, the config-driven
 ;; replacement for the hardcoded client.cljs root branch.
 :seon.config/root-context
 {:seon.agent/ctx
  [{:seon.agent.ctx/name :live-tile :seon.agent.ctx/priority 35
    :seon.render/ai seon.agent.ctx.live-tile/live-tile-block
    :seon.render.live-tile/content seon.render.system/system-view}]}}
